1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,230
Sweetheart, I have cooked Christmas dinner for

2
00:00:03,230 --> 00:00:04,353
sixty-one years.

3
00:00:04,533 --> 00:00:06,578
The first time I was nineteen,

4
00:00:06,578 --> 00:00:09,168
newly married, and I burned the rolls,

5
00:00:09,168 --> 00:00:10,327
forgot the gravy,

6
00:00:10,327 --> 00:00:12,508
and served the turkey raw in the

7
00:00:12,508 --> 00:00:12,985
middle.

8
00:00:13,165 --> 00:00:15,549
I cried in the pantry while my

9
00:00:15,549 --> 00:00:18,726
husband told everybody it was delicious.

10
00:00:18,906 --> 00:00:20,004
So believe me,

11
00:00:20,004 --> 00:00:22,826
every mistake I'm about to tell you,

12
00:00:22,826 --> 00:00:25,962
I either made myself or watched somebody

13
00:00:25,962 --> 00:00:27,138
I love make it.

14
00:00:27,487 --> 00:00:30,382
Tonight I'm giving you the eight Christmas

15
00:00:30,382 --> 00:00:33,140
dinner mistakes I see every single year,

16
00:00:33,140 --> 00:00:34,380
and for every one,

17
00:00:34,380 --> 00:00:36,241
exactly what to do instead.

18
00:00:36,421 --> 00:00:37,852
My mother's way,

19
00:00:37,852 --> 00:00:39,997
and Grandma Pearl's way.

20
00:00:40,177 --> 00:00:42,569
Most of it is just planning.

21
00:00:42,749 --> 00:00:43,837
Get a pencil,

22
00:00:43,837 --> 00:00:44,340
honey.

23
00:00:44,520 --> 00:00:46,612
By the end of this you'll have

24
00:00:46,612 --> 00:00:49,263
a Christmas dinner that comes out hot,

25
00:00:49,263 --> 00:00:51,914
on time, and without anybody crying in

26
00:00:51,914 --> 00:00:52,681
the pantry.

27
00:00:53,031 --> 00:00:54,703
Mistake number one.

28
00:00:54,883 --> 00:00:57,147
Keeping the whole dinner in your head.

29
00:00:57,327 --> 00:00:59,766
You think you remember everything,

30
00:00:59,766 --> 00:01:02,348
and then at four o'clock you realize

31
00:01:02,348 --> 00:01:04,858
the sweet potatoes need the oven at

32
00:01:04,858 --> 00:01:06,866
the same time as the turkey,

33
00:01:06,866 --> 00:01:08,875
and the rolls haven't risen,

34
00:01:08,875 --> 00:01:11,457
and nobody bought cream for the pie.

35
00:01:11,806 --> 00:01:13,362
Do this instead.

36
00:01:13,542 --> 00:01:15,502
Write a timeline on paper,

37
00:01:15,502 --> 00:01:18,442
backwards from the minute you sit down.

38
00:01:18,622 --> 00:01:20,425
If dinner is at three,

39
00:01:20,425 --> 00:01:22,720
the turkey comes out at two.

40
00:01:22,900 --> 00:01:24,595
It goes in at nine.

41
00:01:24,775 --> 00:01:26,842
Potatoes on at one-thirty.

42
00:01:27,022 --> 00:01:29,471
Rolls in when the turkey comes out.

43
00:01:29,651 --> 00:01:32,498
My mother taped her timeline inside the

44
00:01:32,498 --> 00:01:34,689
cupboard door every Christmas,

45
00:01:34,689 --> 00:01:37,317
in pencil, and crossed off each line

46
00:01:37,317 --> 00:01:38,266
with a big X.

47
00:01:38,446 --> 00:01:41,221
I still have one from nineteen fifty-eight.

48
00:01:41,570 --> 00:01:44,137
And make the shopping list from the

49
00:01:44,137 --> 00:01:45,971
recipes, not from memory.

50
00:01:46,151 --> 00:01:48,879
Read every recipe the week before,

51
00:01:48,879 --> 00:01:52,008
every line, and write down every single

52
00:01:52,008 --> 00:01:54,254
thing, even salt and butter.

53
00:01:54,434 --> 00:01:56,762
Butter runs out at Christmas,

54
00:01:56,762 --> 00:01:57,244
honey.

55
00:01:57,424 --> 00:01:59,990
Every year somebody on Elm Street knocked

56
00:01:59,990 --> 00:02:02,181
on our door on Christmas morning to

57
00:02:02,181 --> 00:02:04,184
borrow a stick of butter from my

58
00:02:04,184 --> 00:02:04,622
mother.

59
00:02:04,972 --> 00:02:07,870
And here's the thing nobody tells young

60
00:02:07,870 --> 00:02:08,316
cooks.

61
00:02:08,496 --> 00:02:10,563
Set the table the night before.

62
00:02:10,743 --> 00:02:12,702
Plates, glasses, napkins,

63
00:02:12,702 --> 00:02:13,956
the good silver,

64
00:02:13,956 --> 00:02:16,308
the gravy boat with a spoon in

65
00:02:16,308 --> 00:02:18,895
it, every serving bowl out on the

66
00:02:18,895 --> 00:02:21,638
counter with a little slip of paper

67
00:02:21,638 --> 00:02:23,990
inside saying what goes in it.

68
00:02:24,170 --> 00:02:26,156
My mother did it after we went

69
00:02:26,156 --> 00:02:27,746
to bed on Christmas Eve.

70
00:02:27,926 --> 00:02:30,614
On Christmas Day there's no hunting for

71
00:02:30,614 --> 00:02:33,165
the big platter while the turkey gets

72
00:02:33,165 --> 00:02:33,510
cold.

73
00:02:33,859 --> 00:02:35,520
Mistake number two.

74
00:02:35,700 --> 00:02:38,042
Taking the turkey out of the freezer

75
00:02:38,042 --> 00:02:39,148
on Christmas Eve.

76
00:02:39,328 --> 00:02:41,961
On Christmas morning it's still a block

77
00:02:41,961 --> 00:02:43,378
of ice in the middle,

78
00:02:43,378 --> 00:02:46,079
and people start doing dangerous things,

79
00:02:46,079 --> 00:02:48,172
like leaving it in the sink all

80
00:02:48,172 --> 00:02:50,264
day or putting it in hot water.

81
00:02:50,614 --> 00:02:52,159
Do this instead.

82
00:02:52,339 --> 00:02:54,331
Thaw it in the refrigerator,

83
00:02:54,331 --> 00:02:54,971
in a pan,

84
00:02:54,971 --> 00:02:57,034
and give it one day for every

85
00:02:57,034 --> 00:02:58,457
four or five pounds.

86
00:02:58,637 --> 00:03:01,703
A twenty-pound bird needs four or five

87
00:03:01,703 --> 00:03:04,124
days, so it goes in the icebox

88
00:03:04,124 --> 00:03:06,787
on the Saturday before Christmas.

89
00:03:06,967 --> 00:03:07,950
If you're late,

90
00:03:07,950 --> 00:03:09,784
put it breast down in a sink

91
00:03:09,784 --> 00:03:12,012
of cold water and change the water

92
00:03:12,012 --> 00:03:13,388
every thirty minutes.

93
00:03:13,568 --> 00:03:15,210
Never warm water,

94
00:03:15,210 --> 00:03:16,273
sweetheart.

95
00:03:16,453 --> 00:03:18,020
Never on the counter.

96
00:03:18,369 --> 00:03:19,879
And avoid this,

97
00:03:19,879 --> 00:03:20,482
honey.

98
00:03:20,662 --> 00:03:23,085
Never put stuffing inside a bird the

99
00:03:23,085 --> 00:03:23,960
night before.

100
00:03:24,140 --> 00:03:26,632
Mix the dry and wet parts separately

101
00:03:26,632 --> 00:03:28,640
the night before if you like,

102
00:03:28,640 --> 00:03:31,132
but stuff the turkey right before it

103
00:03:31,132 --> 00:03:32,309
goes in the oven,

104
00:03:32,309 --> 00:03:34,801
and check the middle of the stuffing

105
00:03:34,801 --> 00:03:36,809
gets hot all the way through,

106
00:03:36,809 --> 00:03:39,093
a hundred and sixty-five degrees.

107
00:03:39,273 --> 00:03:40,923
Or do what I do now,

108
00:03:40,923 --> 00:03:43,232
and bake it in its own dish.

109
00:03:43,412 --> 00:03:46,870
It gets that crispy top everybody fights

110
00:03:46,870 --> 00:03:47,302
over.

111
00:03:47,651 --> 00:03:49,969
How do you know the turkey is

112
00:03:49,969 --> 00:03:50,368
done?

113
00:03:50,548 --> 00:03:53,065
Not by the little plastic button,

114
00:03:53,065 --> 00:03:53,903
sweetheart.

115
00:03:54,083 --> 00:03:55,779
Buy a meat thermometer.

116
00:03:55,959 --> 00:03:57,668
Put it in the thickest part of

117
00:03:57,668 --> 00:03:59,720
the thigh without touching the bone.

118
00:03:59,900 --> 00:04:03,098
A hundred and sixty-five degrees and it's

119
00:04:03,098 --> 00:04:03,488
done.

120
00:04:03,668 --> 00:04:06,271
My mother tested by wiggling the leg,

121
00:04:06,271 --> 00:04:08,101
and she was usually right,

122
00:04:08,101 --> 00:04:10,986
but I've had a thermometer since nineteen

123
00:04:10,986 --> 00:04:13,378
seventy and I haven't served a raw

124
00:04:13,378 --> 00:04:16,404
turkey since that first terrible Christmas.

125
00:04:16,753 --> 00:04:18,379
Mistake number three.

126
00:04:18,559 --> 00:04:21,279
Trying to cook every single dish on

127
00:04:21,279 --> 00:04:22,367
Christmas Day.

128
00:04:22,547 --> 00:04:24,185
One oven, one cook,

129
00:04:24,185 --> 00:04:27,029
eight dishes, and a house full of

130
00:04:27,029 --> 00:04:27,632
people.

131
00:04:27,812 --> 00:04:29,941
That's how the rolls burn and the

132
00:04:29,941 --> 00:04:31,748
cook misses the whole party.

133
00:04:32,097 --> 00:04:33,642
Do this instead.

134
00:04:33,822 --> 00:04:36,167
Make everything you can ahead.

135
00:04:36,347 --> 00:04:38,239
Pies on the twenty-third.

136
00:04:38,419 --> 00:04:41,074
Cranberry sauce on the twenty-second,

137
00:04:41,074 --> 00:04:43,586
because it's better after two days.

138
00:04:43,766 --> 00:04:46,167
Cut the onions and celery for the

139
00:04:46,167 --> 00:04:49,004
stuffing the night before and keep them

140
00:04:49,004 --> 00:04:50,314
in a covered bowl.

141
00:04:50,494 --> 00:04:53,361
Make the mashed potatoes in the morning

142
00:04:53,361 --> 00:04:55,641
and keep them warm in a covered

143
00:04:55,641 --> 00:04:57,332
pot set in a pan of hot

144
00:04:57,332 --> 00:04:57,773
water.

145
00:04:57,953 --> 00:05:01,059
Grandma Pearl said the best Christmas cook

146
00:05:01,059 --> 00:05:03,572
is the one who's sitting down when

147
00:05:03,572 --> 00:05:04,977
the doorbell rings.

148
00:05:05,327 --> 00:05:08,242
Here's my mother's cranberry sauce,

149
00:05:08,242 --> 00:05:10,656
honey, it couldn't be easier.

150
00:05:10,836 --> 00:05:13,327
One bag of fresh cranberries,

151
00:05:13,327 --> 00:05:14,787
one cup of sugar,

152
00:05:14,787 --> 00:05:16,247
one cup of water.

153
00:05:16,427 --> 00:05:18,246
Boil the sugar and water,

154
00:05:18,246 --> 00:05:19,410
add the berries,

155
00:05:19,410 --> 00:05:22,103
and cook about ten minutes until they

156
00:05:22,103 --> 00:05:22,394
pop.

157
00:05:22,574 --> 00:05:25,021
Add the grated peel of one orange

158
00:05:25,021 --> 00:05:25,837
at the end.

159
00:05:26,017 --> 00:05:28,021
Pour it in a bowl and put

160
00:05:28,021 --> 00:05:29,384
it in the icebox.

161
00:05:29,564 --> 00:05:31,711
It sets all by itself.

162
00:05:31,891 --> 00:05:34,272
Nobody ever went back to the can

163
00:05:34,272 --> 00:05:35,537
after tasting it.

164
00:05:35,886 --> 00:05:38,786
And use your refrigerator like a second

165
00:05:38,786 --> 00:05:39,381
kitchen.

166
00:05:39,561 --> 00:05:40,857
The week before,

167
00:05:40,857 --> 00:05:42,800
clean it out completely.

168
00:05:42,980 --> 00:05:45,052
Throw away the old jars,

169
00:05:45,052 --> 00:05:46,520
wipe the shelves,

170
00:05:46,520 --> 00:05:47,729
and make room.

171
00:05:47,909 --> 00:05:50,093
You'll need it for the turkey,

172
00:05:50,093 --> 00:05:51,549
the cranberry sauce,

173
00:05:51,549 --> 00:05:54,097
the pies, the cream and the drinks.

174
00:05:54,277 --> 00:05:57,192
My mother called it the Christmas cleaning,

175
00:05:57,192 --> 00:05:59,090
and she did it every year on

176
00:05:59,090 --> 00:06:02,073
the eighteenth, while we kids ate everything

177
00:06:02,073 --> 00:06:03,565
she found in the back.

178
00:06:03,914 --> 00:06:05,737
Mistake number four.

179
00:06:05,917 --> 00:06:08,262
Carving the turkey the minute it comes

180
00:06:08,262 --> 00:06:09,249
out of the oven.

181
00:06:09,429 --> 00:06:12,771
Everybody's hungry, everybody's watching,

182
00:06:12,771 --> 00:06:14,401
so you cut right in,

183
00:06:14,401 --> 00:06:16,927
and all the juice runs out onto

184
00:06:16,927 --> 00:06:17,742
the board.

185
00:06:17,922 --> 00:06:20,079
And the meat on the plate is

186
00:06:20,079 --> 00:06:22,775
dry before anybody even says grace.

187
00:06:23,124 --> 00:06:24,645
Do this instead.

188
00:06:24,825 --> 00:06:26,172
Let it rest.

189
00:06:26,352 --> 00:06:28,821
Cover it loosely with foil and leave

190
00:06:28,821 --> 00:06:30,741
it alone for thirty minutes.

191
00:06:30,921 --> 00:06:31,910
It stays hot,

192
00:06:31,910 --> 00:06:34,499
I promise, and the juice goes back

193
00:06:34,499 --> 00:06:35,565
into the meat.

194
00:06:35,745 --> 00:06:37,974
That half hour is when you make

195
00:06:37,974 --> 00:06:40,348
the gravy, warm the rolls and get

196
00:06:40,348 --> 00:06:42,002
the sides on the table.

197
00:06:42,182 --> 00:06:43,871
My father always carved,

198
00:06:43,871 --> 00:06:46,123
and my mother never let him near

199
00:06:46,123 --> 00:06:48,022
the bird until she said so.

200
00:06:48,202 --> 00:06:50,884
She'd slap his hand with a wooden

201
00:06:50,884 --> 00:06:51,372
spoon.

202
00:06:51,721 --> 00:06:54,016
Here's how to carve so it looks

203
00:06:54,016 --> 00:06:55,274
beautiful, honey.

204
00:06:55,454 --> 00:06:57,901
Don't saw slices off the whole bird

205
00:06:57,901 --> 00:06:58,809
at the table.

206
00:06:58,989 --> 00:07:00,859
Take the bird to the kitchen.

207
00:07:01,039 --> 00:07:03,749
Cut off each leg and each breast

208
00:07:03,749 --> 00:07:04,765
half, whole.

209
00:07:04,945 --> 00:07:07,754
Then slice the breast across the grain,

210
00:07:07,754 --> 00:07:09,699
about as thick as a pencil,

211
00:07:09,699 --> 00:07:11,715
and lay the slices on a warm

212
00:07:11,715 --> 00:07:14,164
platter with the legs at the ends.

213
00:07:14,344 --> 00:07:16,596
Put a little parsley around it.

214
00:07:16,776 --> 00:07:18,835
It looks like a magazine,

215
00:07:18,835 --> 00:07:21,141
and it stays warm and juicy.

216
00:07:21,492 --> 00:07:23,314
Mistake number five.

217
00:07:23,494 --> 00:07:26,999
Dumping flour straight into hot drippings and

218
00:07:26,999 --> 00:07:28,556
hoping for the best.

219
00:07:28,736 --> 00:07:31,057
You get lumps the size of marbles,

220
00:07:31,057 --> 00:07:33,514
and then somebody pours it through a

221
00:07:33,514 --> 00:07:36,040
strainer, and there's half as much as

222
00:07:36,040 --> 00:07:36,654
you need.

223
00:07:37,005 --> 00:07:38,525
Do this instead.

224
00:07:38,705 --> 00:07:40,517
Grandma Pearl's way.

225
00:07:40,697 --> 00:07:42,802
Put a quarter cup of flour in

226
00:07:42,802 --> 00:07:44,544
a jar with a cup of cold

227
00:07:44,544 --> 00:07:46,141
water, put the lid on,

228
00:07:46,141 --> 00:07:47,447
and shake it hard,

229
00:07:47,447 --> 00:07:49,044
like you're mad at it.

230
00:07:49,224 --> 00:07:51,603
Then pour it slowly into the hot

231
00:07:51,603 --> 00:07:53,462
drippings while you stir,

232
00:07:53,462 --> 00:07:56,287
and keep stirring until it bubbles and

233
00:07:56,287 --> 00:07:56,956
thickens.

234
00:07:57,136 --> 00:07:59,052
Salt and pepper at the end.

235
00:07:59,232 --> 00:08:01,228
Cold water and a jar,

236
00:08:01,228 --> 00:08:01,798
honey.

237
00:08:01,978 --> 00:08:04,287
In sixty years I've never had a

238
00:08:04,287 --> 00:08:04,660
lump.

239
00:08:05,010 --> 00:08:07,395
And never throw away the drippings,

240
00:08:07,395 --> 00:08:08,144
sweetheart.

241
00:08:08,324 --> 00:08:09,976
If there's too much fat,

242
00:08:09,976 --> 00:08:12,729
pour everything into a measuring cup and

243
00:08:12,729 --> 00:08:14,106
let it sit a minute.

244
00:08:14,286 --> 00:08:16,411
The fat rises to the top.

245
00:08:16,591 --> 00:08:19,147
Spoon it off and keep the brown

246
00:08:19,147 --> 00:08:20,550
juice underneath.

247
00:08:20,730 --> 00:08:23,605
That brown juice is the whole flavor

248
00:08:23,605 --> 00:08:24,723
of your gravy.

249
00:08:24,903 --> 00:08:26,873
The fat my mother saved in a

250
00:08:26,873 --> 00:08:28,069
can by the stove,

251
00:08:28,069 --> 00:08:30,531
for frying potatoes the rest of the

252
00:08:30,531 --> 00:08:30,883
week.

253
00:08:31,063 --> 00:08:32,433
Nothing wasted.

254
00:08:32,783 --> 00:08:34,640
Mistake number six.

255
00:08:34,820 --> 00:08:38,168
Trying four new recipes from a magazine

256
00:08:38,168 --> 00:08:39,627
on Christmas Day.

257
00:08:39,807 --> 00:08:42,698
Christmas is not the day to experiment.

258
00:08:42,878 --> 00:08:44,657
If something goes wrong,

259
00:08:44,657 --> 00:08:46,585
there's no time to fix it,

260
00:08:46,585 --> 00:08:49,255
and the family wanted the old dishes

261
00:08:49,255 --> 00:08:49,774
anyway.

262
00:08:50,124 --> 00:08:51,552
Do this instead.

263
00:08:51,732 --> 00:08:52,909
One new dish,

264
00:08:52,909 --> 00:08:55,355
at most, and try it once in

265
00:08:55,355 --> 00:08:57,258
early December first.

266
00:08:57,438 --> 00:09:00,148
Everything else should be the dishes the

267
00:09:00,148 --> 00:09:01,977
family has eaten for years.

268
00:09:02,157 --> 00:09:04,758
That's what Christmas tastes like.

269
00:09:04,938 --> 00:09:07,721
My grandchildren would riot if I didn't

270
00:09:07,721 --> 00:09:10,790
make Pearl's sweet potatoes with the little

271
00:09:10,790 --> 00:09:12,218
marshmallows on top.

272
00:09:12,398 --> 00:09:15,323
Nobody remembers the fancy new salad.

273
00:09:15,503 --> 00:09:18,162
They remember what tastes like home.

274
00:09:18,512 --> 00:09:20,893
Here's Pearl's sweet potatoes,

275
00:09:20,893 --> 00:09:22,877
so you can make them too.

276
00:09:23,057 --> 00:09:25,895
Boil four big sweet potatoes in their

277
00:09:25,895 --> 00:09:27,199
skins until soft,

278
00:09:27,199 --> 00:09:29,730
peel them and mash them with half

279
00:09:29,730 --> 00:09:31,111
a stick of butter,

280
00:09:31,111 --> 00:09:33,028
a third of a cup of brown

281
00:09:33,028 --> 00:09:35,176
sugar, a pinch of salt and a

282
00:09:35,176 --> 00:09:36,710
little orange juice.

283
00:09:36,890 --> 00:09:39,016
Spread them in a buttered dish,

284
00:09:39,016 --> 00:09:41,690
cover the top with little marshmallows,

285
00:09:41,690 --> 00:09:43,953
and bake at three fifty until the

286
00:09:43,953 --> 00:09:45,667
marshmallows turn golden.

287
00:09:45,847 --> 00:09:47,554
Watch them, honey.

288
00:09:47,734 --> 00:09:49,116
They burn in a blink.

289
00:09:49,466 --> 00:09:51,219
Mistake number seven.

290
00:09:51,399 --> 00:09:53,779
Being the only one in the kitchen.

291
00:09:53,959 --> 00:09:56,272
The cook works for two days and

292
00:09:56,272 --> 00:09:58,661
everybody else watches football.

293
00:09:58,841 --> 00:10:01,504
Then she's too tired to enjoy any

294
00:10:01,504 --> 00:10:03,684
of it, and too proud to say

295
00:10:03,684 --> 00:10:03,926
so.

296
00:10:04,276 --> 00:10:05,692
Do this instead.

297
00:10:05,872 --> 00:10:07,779
Give everybody a job,

298
00:10:07,779 --> 00:10:08,960
written down.

299
00:10:09,140 --> 00:10:11,908
Danny and I peeled potatoes from the

300
00:10:11,908 --> 00:10:13,215
time we were six.

301
00:10:13,395 --> 00:10:15,787
My father set the table and filled

302
00:10:15,787 --> 00:10:17,052
the water glasses.

303
00:10:17,232 --> 00:10:19,880
Grandma Pearl made the gravy.

304
00:10:20,060 --> 00:10:23,095
When guests ask what they can bring,

305
00:10:23,095 --> 00:10:23,938
say a pie,

306
00:10:23,938 --> 00:10:26,130
or rolls, or a bag of ice,

307
00:10:26,130 --> 00:10:27,142
and mean it.

308
00:10:27,322 --> 00:10:29,255
And the rule in my house is

309
00:10:29,255 --> 00:10:32,047
simple: the cook doesn't do the dishes.

310
00:10:32,227 --> 00:10:34,342
Whoever didn't cook,

311
00:10:34,342 --> 00:10:35,083
washes.

312
00:10:35,263 --> 00:10:38,171
That rule has saved more marriages than

313
00:10:38,171 --> 00:10:39,141
any preacher.

314
00:10:39,491 --> 00:10:41,538
And don't forget the cook,

315
00:10:41,538 --> 00:10:42,405
sweetheart.

316
00:10:42,585 --> 00:10:45,523
Make yourself a plate before the platter

317
00:10:45,523 --> 00:10:47,727
goes around, and set it aside,

318
00:10:47,727 --> 00:10:49,784
or you'll end up with a wing

319
00:10:49,784 --> 00:10:51,106
and cold potatoes.

320
00:10:51,286 --> 00:10:53,860
And sit down with everybody for the

321
00:10:53,860 --> 00:10:54,375
prayer.

322
00:10:54,555 --> 00:10:57,185
My mother always stood in the kitchen

323
00:10:57,185 --> 00:10:58,677
doorway during grace,

324
00:10:58,677 --> 00:11:00,881
and one year my father went and

325
00:11:00,881 --> 00:11:03,013
got her chair and put it right

326
00:11:03,013 --> 00:11:03,866
next to his.

327
00:11:04,046 --> 00:11:06,453
She sat in it every Christmas after

328
00:11:06,453 --> 00:11:06,797
that.

329
00:11:07,148 --> 00:11:08,634
Mistake number eight.

330
00:11:08,814 --> 00:11:10,951
Throwing out half the turkey on the

331
00:11:10,951 --> 00:11:11,867
twenty-seventh.

332
00:11:12,047 --> 00:11:13,812
In nineteen fifty-one,

333
00:11:13,812 --> 00:11:16,540
nobody I knew wasted a single bite

334
00:11:16,540 --> 00:11:18,305
of a Christmas turkey.

335
00:11:18,485 --> 00:11:20,865
A bird was too expensive.

336
00:11:21,045 --> 00:11:22,972
It fed us for a week.

337
00:11:23,322 --> 00:11:24,831
Do this instead.

338
00:11:25,011 --> 00:11:26,925
Within two hours of dinner,

339
00:11:26,925 --> 00:11:29,122
take the meat off the bones and

340
00:11:29,122 --> 00:11:31,603
put it in shallow covered dishes in

341
00:11:31,603 --> 00:11:32,383
the icebox.

342
00:11:32,563 --> 00:11:34,536
Eat it within four days,

343
00:11:34,536 --> 00:11:35,605
or freeze it.

344
00:11:35,785 --> 00:11:38,328
Then put the carcass in your biggest

345
00:11:38,328 --> 00:11:39,600
pot with an onion,

346
00:11:39,600 --> 00:11:41,578
two carrots and some celery,

347
00:11:41,578 --> 00:11:43,910
cover it with water and simmer it

348
00:11:43,910 --> 00:11:44,899
all afternoon.

349
00:11:45,079 --> 00:11:47,589
That's your soup for the cold week

350
00:11:47,589 --> 00:11:48,771
after Christmas.

351
00:11:48,951 --> 00:11:51,170
My mother called it the best meal

352
00:11:51,170 --> 00:11:52,582
of the whole holiday,

353
00:11:52,582 --> 00:11:53,792
and she was right.

354
00:11:54,143 --> 00:11:56,185
So here's the whole lesson,

355
00:11:56,185 --> 00:11:56,639
honey.

356
00:11:56,819 --> 00:11:58,549
Plan it on paper.

357
00:11:58,729 --> 00:12:00,679
Thaw the bird early.

358
00:12:00,859 --> 00:12:01,869
Cook ahead.

359
00:12:02,049 --> 00:12:03,767
Let the turkey rest.

360
00:12:03,947 --> 00:12:05,921
Shake the gravy in a jar.

361
00:12:06,101 --> 00:12:08,063
One new dish at most.

362
00:12:08,243 --> 00:12:10,020
Give everybody a job.

363
00:12:10,200 --> 00:12:12,638
And make soup from the bones.

364
00:12:12,818 --> 00:12:15,020
Do those eight things and you'll be

365
00:12:15,020 --> 00:12:17,473
the calmest person in your own kitchen.

366
00:12:17,824 --> 00:12:20,041
And tell me in the comments,

367
00:12:20,041 --> 00:12:20,912
sweetheart.

368
00:12:21,092 --> 00:12:23,601
What's the one dish your family would

369
00:12:23,601 --> 00:12:25,364
riot without at Christmas?

370
00:12:25,544 --> 00:12:27,239
I read every one.

371
00:12:27,419 --> 00:12:29,796
Tomorrow I'll tell you how to wrap

372
00:12:29,796 --> 00:12:31,753
presents for almost nothing,

373
00:12:31,753 --> 00:12:34,269
so pretty nobody wants to open them.

374
00:12:34,449 --> 00:12:36,156
Good night, honey.

375
00:12:36,336 --> 00:12:37,764
Merry Christmas.
